  "Question": "Leah has \\(13\\) coins, all of which are pennies and nickels. If she had one more nickel than she has now, then she would have the same number of pennies and nickels. In cents, how much are Leah’s coins worth?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(33\\)",
    "B": "\\(35\\)",
    "C": "\\(37\\)",
    "D": "\\(39\\)",
    "E": "\\(41\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Adding one nickel would give Leah \\(13+1=14\\) coins, with equal numbers of pennies and nickels. Each kind would therefore have \\(14\\div2=7\\) coins.\n\nRemoving that extra nickel leaves 7 pennies and 6 nickels. Since a penny is worth 1 cent and a nickel is worth 5 cents, the actual value is\n\\[\n7\\cdot1+6\\cdot5=37\\text{ cents}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{37}\\) cents, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
